    "note": "Introduced version; no votes on file. SECTION 3 (ORS 166.274) adds this conviction to the bars from which a person may petition for relief. The gun ban is a small part of a bill mostly about the new threat crime."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 2 (ORS 166.250): Except as otherwise provided in this section or ORS 166.260, 166.270, 166.273, 166.274, 166.291, 166.292 or 166.410 to 166.470, a person commits the crime of unlawful possession of a firearm if the person knowingly: … Has been convicted of threatening a mass injury event under section 1 of this 2024 Act; or\nSECTION 2 (ORS 166.250): Unlawful possession of a firearm is a Class A misdemeanor."
